{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Have you kept alive every female, etc.</b> It appears that this error came to them because they already knew the commandment, ״לֹא יָבֹא עַמּוֹנִי וּמוֹאָבִי״ and so forth — an Ammonite man but not an Ammonite woman (Yevamot 60b), because it is not the way of women to go forth with bread and water. And it is known that the essential reason for their exclusion is because they caused Israel to sin through harlotry, and the matter is contingent upon the fact that they did not greet them with bread and water — for this depends on that: that is the reason they did not greet them with bread and water, so that they would be hungry and also thirsty from the exertion of the journey, and they would be compelled to eat from the sacrifices of their gods and to drink from the strained wine, in order to accustom them to licentiousness, as is concluded in Sanhedrin (106a). And even though in the matter of harlotry the women were the principal ones, nevertheless the women were not excluded, because the entire essence of this deed was done by the men — for they were the ones who made their daughters available and forced them into harlotry, for whatever they did, they did by the command of their husbands or their fathers. And from here this error went forth for them, to say: just as the women of Ammon and Moab were not excluded from entering the congregation of HaShem even though they were the agents of the harlotry, so too in the wars of Midian they were not commanded to kill the women, for they were compelled in everything they did. And Moses said to them: ״הֵן הֵנָּה הָיוּ״ and so forth — true, the commandment regarding Ammon and Moab for all generations is a ruling not to penalize the women, for the reason that has been explained; but in the case of Midian, whom you were commanded to kill, all the more so are the women included, in the manner that it says (Leviticus 20:15): ״וְאֶת הַבְּהֵמָה תַּהֲרֹגוּ״, and the reason is because an animal came to a man as a stumbling block through it; so too the women, for they themselves were to the children of Israel a stone of striking and a stumbling block, and you should have learned from the law of the animal to the law of these women." "And above, in the portion of Pinchas (25:17), we explained that the reason He did not command to destroy Moab is because the children of Israel initiated the corruption and went to the daughters of Moab to entice them, as it is written (Numbers 25:1): ״וַיָּחֶל הָעָם לִזְנוֹת אֶל בְּנוֹת מוֹאָב״ — but the daughters of Midian are enemies to you, for they came to you, as we demonstrated all of this with proofs. And it may be that on account of this Moses spoke to nullify their error: ״הֵן הֵנָּה הָיוּ לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — for they went to the children of Israel to entice them, and they are not like the daughters of Moab, for therefore the women were not excluded from entering the congregation of HaShem, because they were not the initiators. But the daughters of Midian — they themselves were the ones who initiated the corruption against the children of Israel, as has been said."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:43:44.800462340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}